{
    "title": "Employee Wellbeing, Safety Incidents, and Female Wages",
    "summary": "The page covers Principle 3 on employee wellbeing, including spending on wellbeing measures as a percentage of revenue for FY 2024-25 (0.17%) and the previous 15-month FY (0.13%), with costs covering accident insurance, health insurance, maternity/paternity benefits, daycare, and other physical/mental wellbeing initiatives. It lists safety-related incidents (LTIFR, total recordable injuries, fatalities, high-consequence injuries) for employees and workers, including contract workforce, for both periods, and notes investigations to prevent recurrence. Principle 5 on human rights reports gross wages paid to females as a percentage of total wages (15% in both periods).",
}
